<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<!--
SPDX-FileCopyrightText: 2026 Vladislav Janeček
SPDX-License-Identifier: GPL-3.0-or-later

The entitlements macos/Makefile signs into the bundle. They count under the
hardened runtime of a Developer ID build, which lets an app send Apple
events to another app only with the first one: Settings → AI asks Claude
Desktop to quit before it rewrites its configuration
(NSRunningApplication.terminate, a quit event; ClaudeDesktopService).
NSAppleEventsUsageDescription in Info.plist.in is the reason macOS shows if
it asks the user. No App Sandbox (docs/macos-port.md §12).
-->
<!DOCTYPE plist PUBLIC "-//Apple//DTD PLIST 1.0//EN" "http://www.apple.com/DTDs/PropertyList-1.0.dtd">
<plist version="1.0">
<dict>
	<key>com.apple.security.automation.apple-events</key>
	<true/>
</dict>
</plist>
